aws "why drawing instructions and not pixels?"
awt (jy aws)
awu "array"
awv (awu)
aww "Initially, I tried to communicate with the outside world using pixel graphics. However, I believe that's not the right move as pixels are more difficult to handle in code. Having pixels (or some concept ofa texture) within this notebook requires either:\n- mutable values (which don't exist in here), or\n- lots of copying on every texture modification, or\n- a super-smart optimizing compiler (which is useful but it has the sort of slow-by-default-and-you-have-to-trust-the-black-box-to-work feeling I don't like), or\n- inefficient storage of individual pixels in trees."
awx (jy aww)
awy (avt awx)
awz "By communicating the intent on a quite high-level, we can instead make use of GPUs when turning the high-level drawing instructions into pixels. This is also similar to how Flutter works: The Dart VM is decently fast, but not super fast, so it just emits drawing instructions that the lower-level C++ engine takes and turns into pixels."
